CMB GitHub Integration (Final Form)

1. Core Principle

A GitHub link becomes a usable file.Nothing more.Nothing less.

GitHub URL → raw file → viewer loads it

Everything else is optional.

2. Access Modes

A. Public URL → Raw

GitHub “blob” links aren’t real files.Convert them to “raw” and load.

blob → raw → playable

No API.No tokens.No authentication.

B. Local Clone

If the repo is on disk, read it directly.

~/Projects/Emphemsa/

Viewer reads:

output/

data/

blueprints/

.git (optional)

Zero latency.Zero friction.

3. Automatic File Pairing

Load a video:

run_001.mp4

Viewer looks for:

run_001.data.json
run_001.cmb

If found → attach.If not → play video alone.

No config.No mapping files.Just filename matching.

4. UI Requirements

Only two buttons:

Open from GitHub URL

Open Local Repo

Everything else is optional sugar.

5. Optional Version Awareness

If .git exists:

read branch

read commit

read tag

If not, ignore.

Display:

main@a1b2c3d

Done.



